1
00:00:01,914 --> 00:00:03,699
[instrumental music]

2
00:00:03,786 --> 00:00:05,396
[door closes]

3
00:00:13,274 --> 00:00:15,537
- Hey, you.
- Hi.

4
00:00:15,624 --> 00:00:16,538
[footsteps]

5
00:00:18,409 --> 00:00:19,845
- Oh, hey.
- Hey, thought you'd gone home.

6
00:00:19,932 --> 00:00:21,151
I wish.
We're up.

7
00:00:21,238 --> 00:00:22,935
There's a double
homicide in Rancho Rosa.

8
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:24,111
Local sheriff's
in over his head.

9
00:00:24,198 --> 00:00:26,374
- I'm on it.
- Boss.

10
00:00:26,461 --> 00:00:28,680
You've been promising
me more time in the field.

11
00:00:28,767 --> 00:00:31,379
- Now's as good a time as any.
- You're right.

12
00:00:31,466 --> 00:00:32,902
Rigsby, be a cover
in the office on this one.

13
00:00:33,642 --> 00:00:34,817
Let's go.

14
00:00:37,341 --> 00:00:38,560
You're okay with this,
I hope?

15
00:00:38,647 --> 00:00:39,909
Absolutely, yeah.

16
00:00:46,829 --> 00:00:49,875
[police radio]

17
00:00:49,962 --> 00:00:51,094
[indistinct conversations]

18
00:00:53,575 --> 00:00:54,706
[Patrick]
'What's going on?'

19
00:00:54,793 --> 00:00:55,751
Looks like two bullets

20
00:00:55,838 --> 00:00:57,405
to the chest for each of them.

21
00:00:57,492 --> 00:00:58,667
Freshness of the wounds
suggests

22
00:00:58,754 --> 00:01:00,016
it happened
in the last few hours.

23
00:01:00,103 --> 00:01:03,150
Selby and Jana Vickers,
33 and 31 years old

24
00:01:03,237 --> 00:01:04,847
from here in Rancho Rosa.

25
00:01:04,934 --> 00:01:07,241
Sheriff ID'd them
from their driver's licenses.

26
00:01:07,328 --> 00:01:09,939
- Who found the bodies?
- 'Couple of teenagers.'

27
00:01:10,026 --> 00:01:12,028
This place is a local lover's
lane, apparently.

28
00:01:12,115 --> 00:01:13,856
Thieves know that, too.

29
00:01:13,943 --> 00:01:16,467
Sheriff thinks that
it's a robbery gone sour.

30
00:01:16,554 --> 00:01:19,035
Little old to be necking,
aren't they?

31
00:01:19,122 --> 00:01:20,776
There's an age limit on that?

32
00:01:20,863 --> 00:01:23,300
Plus their clothes aren't,
you know, disheveled.

33
00:01:24,214 --> 00:01:25,259
Good point.

34
00:01:25,346 --> 00:01:26,999
Oh, there's a little

35
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:30,481
white thing there sticking
out from Jana's dress.

36
00:01:30,568 --> 00:01:32,092
'Could you just..
Yeah that's it.'

37
00:01:35,138 --> 00:01:36,661
- $800 dress.
- Aha!

38
00:01:38,185 --> 00:01:40,317
Is that a useful "aha"
or an irritating "aha"?

39
00:01:42,145 --> 00:01:45,105
The borrowed dress tells us
they were going somewhere fancy

40
00:01:45,192 --> 00:01:46,410
and wanted to make
an impression.

41
00:01:46,497 --> 00:01:48,238
Not usually
something they'd go for

42
00:01:48,325 --> 00:01:50,110
or they'd have
a later model car.

43
00:01:51,415 --> 00:01:52,982
He needed a few pulls
on the scotch

44
00:01:53,069 --> 00:01:54,462
just to take the edge off

45
00:01:54,549 --> 00:01:57,029
because he was nervous
about who was gonna be there

46
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,770
which in a small town
like this

47
00:01:58,857 --> 00:02:01,730
likely means relatives
or people from his past.

48
00:02:03,253 --> 00:02:05,342
Uh, wedding, maybe?
Or birthday party?

49
00:02:05,429 --> 00:02:06,822
No gift, which leaves..

50
00:02:06,909 --> 00:02:09,825
- No guessing games.
- Aye..

51
00:02:09,912 --> 00:02:13,611
Excuse me, sheriff, what's the
name of the local high school?

52
00:02:13,698 --> 00:02:15,178
[Martha Wash singing
"Everybody Dance Now"]
♪ Everybody dance now ♪♪

53
00:02:17,528 --> 00:02:19,617
[indistinct conversations]

54
00:02:21,576 --> 00:02:22,707
Stephanie?

55
00:02:24,666 --> 00:02:26,233
Oh, my God.
You look fantastic.

56
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:29,061
I'm sorry.
I'm not Stephanie.

57
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,194
Whoa.

58
00:02:31,281 --> 00:02:33,196
Do that again,
and I'll arrest you.

59
00:02:33,283 --> 00:02:36,330
Sorry, I-I had to.
You've always been the one.

60
00:02:36,417 --> 00:02:38,549
[men laughing]
No way.

61
00:02:41,596 --> 00:02:42,727
I'm not the one.

62
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:45,817
[sighs]

63
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,169
[indistinct conversations]

64
00:02:53,216 --> 00:02:54,261
[Patrick]
'High school.'

65
00:02:54,348 --> 00:02:55,653
Best years of your life.

66
00:02:56,959 --> 00:02:57,960
Huh?

67
00:02:58,047 --> 00:03:00,441
[theme music]

68
00:03:10,277 --> 00:03:11,495
[indistinct conversations]

69
00:03:11,582 --> 00:03:13,410
Welcome back
to Rancho Rosa High.

70
00:03:13,497 --> 00:03:15,020
Go, Toros!

71
00:03:15,107 --> 00:03:17,371
I'm Tess, one of your student
ambassadors this weekend.

72
00:03:18,415 --> 00:03:20,722
Nametags and reunion books.

73
00:03:20,809 --> 00:03:22,506
We're with the California Bureau
Of Investigation.

74
00:03:24,116 --> 00:03:26,597
We need to know
if Jana and Selby Vickers

75
00:03:26,684 --> 00:03:28,469
were expected here tonight.

76
00:03:28,556 --> 00:03:30,079
Um..

77
00:03:30,166 --> 00:03:32,212
Yeah, Selby Vickers
and his wife Jana.

78
00:03:33,517 --> 00:03:35,519
They also replied "yes"
to tomorrow's

79
00:03:35,606 --> 00:03:38,609
homecoming picnic and dance.
Is everything okay?

80
00:03:38,696 --> 00:03:41,308
Oh, we need to talk to somebody
who would know them.

81
00:03:42,918 --> 00:03:44,267
Um...

82
00:03:44,354 --> 00:03:45,964
Red-headed woman,
that's Willa Brock.

83
00:03:46,051 --> 00:03:48,010
'She's the reunion
committee chair.'

84
00:03:48,097 --> 00:03:49,620
You didn't really think
we were young enough

85
00:03:49,707 --> 00:03:51,709
to be in this class
when we walked in, did you?

86
00:03:51,796 --> 00:03:54,582
Oh, everyone over the age of 21
looks the same to me.

87
00:03:54,669 --> 00:03:56,018
Tactful and evasive.

88
00:03:56,105 --> 00:03:58,412
You're gonna do very well
in life, Tess.

89
00:03:58,499 --> 00:03:59,413
Go, Toros.

90
00:04:01,458 --> 00:04:03,025
I'm stunned.

91
00:04:03,112 --> 00:04:06,550
I mean, it was surprising enough
Selby was even coming.

92
00:04:06,637 --> 00:04:09,205
- Now this?
- Oh, why the surprise?

93
00:04:09,292 --> 00:04:11,251
Well, he wasn't at the fifth
or the tenth.

94
00:04:12,730 --> 00:04:15,167
- Because..
- Because he was expelled.

95
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:17,735
And never graduated.

96
00:04:17,822 --> 00:04:20,477
'Selby pulled this,
this really nasty prank.'

97
00:04:20,564 --> 00:04:22,000
- What was it, senior year?
- Yeah.

98
00:04:22,087 --> 00:04:24,046
It was his one and only,
Vice Principal DeSouza

99
00:04:24,133 --> 00:04:25,743
caught him, gave him
the ol' boot.

100
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,223
What was the prank?

101
00:04:27,310 --> 00:04:29,921
Uh, there was this,
shall we say

102
00:04:30,008 --> 00:04:33,273
socially challenged boy
named Derek Logan.

103
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,405
Selby dragged him
into the girls' locker room

104
00:04:35,492 --> 00:04:37,538
he blindfolded him
with his own underwear

105
00:04:37,625 --> 00:04:39,844
tied him up, naked

106
00:04:39,931 --> 00:04:41,846
took his picture and then
posted it all over the school.

107
00:04:41,933 --> 00:04:44,066
I mean, how sick
is that, right?

108
00:04:44,153 --> 00:04:46,808
It was disturbing.

109
00:04:46,895 --> 00:04:50,551
Hmm. Uh, is there anything else
you can tell us about him?

110
00:04:50,638 --> 00:04:52,770
'I played football.'
Starting running back.

111
00:04:52,857 --> 00:04:54,337
People around here
are still talking about

112
00:04:54,424 --> 00:04:56,470
the five touchdowns
I scored against Stratton.

113
00:04:56,557 --> 00:04:58,907
What does that
have to do with Selby?

114
00:04:58,994 --> 00:05:00,430
'I was popular.'

115
00:05:00,517 --> 00:05:02,998
I was a jock.
He was a nobody.

116
00:05:03,085 --> 00:05:05,740
I don't know
what kind of person he was.

117
00:05:05,827 --> 00:05:07,698
How about his current life?

118
00:05:07,785 --> 00:05:10,571
I got nada. I got out of
this town as fast as I could.

119
00:05:10,658 --> 00:05:12,355
I live down
in Newport Beach now.

120
00:05:12,442 --> 00:05:13,356
Hmm.

121
00:05:14,575 --> 00:05:15,663
How about you, Willa?

122
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,317
Have you heard anything
about Selby?

123
00:05:17,404 --> 00:05:20,755
Oh, I host a daytime
talk show in Chicago

124
00:05:20,842 --> 00:05:24,019
that tapes two shows a day
and is about to go national.

125
00:05:24,106 --> 00:05:27,196
I'm lucky if I hear anything
about my own family.

126
00:05:27,283 --> 00:05:30,025
Uh, Derek Logan, the kid
that Selby pulled the prank on.

127
00:05:30,112 --> 00:05:31,983
Could you
point him out to us?

128
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:33,333
[Gabe]
'Derek Logan?'

129
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,683
He's not here, is he?
No way!

130
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:38,468
Gabe, it's so good
to see you again.

131
00:05:40,122 --> 00:05:41,602
You almost didn't.

132
00:05:41,689 --> 00:05:44,039
Five hours I spent
on the 101 driving here.

133
00:05:44,126 --> 00:05:47,042
CBI agent Teresa Lisbon,
Patrick Jane.

134
00:05:47,129 --> 00:05:48,783
- This is Gabe Nyland.
- Hi.

135
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:50,698
DA for San Diego County.

136
00:05:50,785 --> 00:05:52,264
'And you've prosecuted
a couple of cases for us.'

137
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:53,483
And now candidate

138
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,529
for lieutenant governor
of California.

139
00:05:55,616 --> 00:05:57,531
Give me the word, G,
I start twisting arms for you

140
00:05:57,618 --> 00:05:59,576
on election day, huh?

141
00:05:59,663 --> 00:06:02,449
Um, Gabe, Selby Vickers
and his wife

142
00:06:02,536 --> 00:06:06,888
were found murdered
at the Glen, shot in their car.

143
00:06:06,975 --> 00:06:08,629
My, god.

144
00:06:08,716 --> 00:06:11,719
I hadn't even heard that name
in 15 years till tonight.

145
00:06:11,806 --> 00:06:12,807
Any idea who did this?

146
00:06:12,894 --> 00:06:15,026
It's early
in the investigation.

147
00:06:15,113 --> 00:06:17,289
- Hey, you just got here, right?
- Yes.

148
00:06:17,377 --> 00:06:19,030
So how is it that you knew
Derek Logan wasn't here?

149
00:06:20,815 --> 00:06:22,556
Well, Derek left the school
and moved out of state

150
00:06:22,643 --> 00:06:25,080
after that prank Selby pulled.

151
00:06:25,167 --> 00:06:27,778
- Word is, he killed himself.
- 'Are you serious?'

152
00:06:27,865 --> 00:06:30,390
I heard he was a blackjack
dealer at a casino.

153
00:06:30,477 --> 00:06:32,261
Uh, we'd like to talk
to some classmates

154
00:06:32,348 --> 00:06:33,784
that still live in the area.

155
00:06:33,871 --> 00:06:35,220
Maybe they know something
about Selby.

156
00:06:35,307 --> 00:06:36,744
Well, there are only a few

157
00:06:36,831 --> 00:06:38,789
but, uh,
the student ambassadors

158
00:06:38,876 --> 00:06:41,357
can probably point you
in the right direction.

159
00:06:41,444 --> 00:06:42,663
Thank you for your time.

160
00:06:43,446 --> 00:06:44,621
[intense music]

161
00:06:47,276 --> 00:06:48,712
Nothing jumps out on this
but I'm gonna have

162
00:06:48,799 --> 00:06:50,845
the tech guys
give it a once-over.

163
00:06:50,932 --> 00:06:52,890
Mail's all big bills
and small bank accounts.

164
00:06:52,977 --> 00:06:54,370
They certainly weren't
living the high life here.

165
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:58,722
They didn't need to.
This was home. They were happy.

166
00:06:58,809 --> 00:07:03,901
[cell phone ringing]
Agent Grace Van Pelt.

167
00:07:03,988 --> 00:07:06,730
[Rigsby on phone]
'Hey. So I got you next of kin
info on Selby.'

168
00:07:06,817 --> 00:07:10,125
Uh, mother in Rancho Rosa.
No luck on Jana, though.

169
00:07:10,212 --> 00:07:11,387
Thanks.
Text me the address?

170
00:07:11,474 --> 00:07:13,258
'Will do.'

171
00:07:13,345 --> 00:07:14,825
So I've never been
to Rancho Rosa before.

172
00:07:14,912 --> 00:07:15,913
What's it like?

173
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,524
Nothing special.
A town.

174
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,919
Cool. What are
you guys doing now?

175
00:07:22,006 --> 00:07:23,878
You know, investigating.

176
00:07:23,965 --> 00:07:26,097
Van pelt, come here.
Check this out.

177
00:07:26,184 --> 00:07:27,272
- I gotta go.
- Y-yeah.

178
00:07:27,359 --> 00:07:29,144
I'm-I'm busy...too.

179
00:07:32,364 --> 00:07:33,844
[exhales deeply]

180
00:07:38,327 --> 00:07:41,461
[Cho]
'This is from
yesterday morning.'

181
00:07:41,548 --> 00:07:43,854
[man on the phone recorder]
'I'm done playing games here.
You hear me?'

182
00:07:43,941 --> 00:07:45,639
'Either you get me my money
or I'm gonna be forced'

183
00:07:45,726 --> 00:07:47,075
'to take action.'

184
00:07:47,162 --> 00:07:48,990
[beeping]
So much for happiness.

185
00:07:49,077 --> 00:07:51,601
Mm.

186
00:07:51,688 --> 00:07:54,996
So you haven't seen Selby
once in all these years?

187
00:07:55,083 --> 00:07:57,520
Supermarket,
movie theater maybe?

188
00:07:57,607 --> 00:08:00,697
No. I mean, you know,
if I did, I-I don't remember.

189
00:08:00,784 --> 00:08:01,698
Hard to believe you, Stu.

190
00:08:03,439 --> 00:08:04,484
I'm sorry?

191
00:08:04,571 --> 00:08:06,790
Well, uh, really?
Okay.

192
00:08:06,877 --> 00:08:08,618
Yeah?
The hair plugs, the heels

193
00:08:08,705 --> 00:08:12,100
this, uh,
professional woman here

194
00:08:12,187 --> 00:08:13,231
posing as your girlfriend..

195
00:08:13,318 --> 00:08:14,537
Wait, wait.
What did you just say?

196
00:08:14,624 --> 00:08:15,973
- Whoa.
- D-did he just call me..

197
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:17,235
- What did you say..
- I-I mean..

198
00:08:17,322 --> 00:08:18,759
That's all we need
for your time.

199
00:08:18,846 --> 00:08:20,543
- I mean, all the questions.
- Beg my pardon.

200
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:22,153
That's all we have for now.
Thank you.

201
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,895
I think you look lovely.
Have a good evening.

202
00:08:24,982 --> 00:08:26,114
Go, Toros.

203
00:08:28,638 --> 00:08:29,726
What's your problem?

204
00:08:31,249 --> 00:08:32,468
Uh, it's just a room

205
00:08:32,555 --> 00:08:34,992
full of people lying
to each other.

206
00:08:35,079 --> 00:08:38,082
Everyone here is trying so hard
to show how much they've changed

207
00:08:38,169 --> 00:08:40,563
when the mere effort
screams that they haven't.

208
00:08:41,651 --> 00:08:43,131
Or they actually
do change

209
00:08:43,218 --> 00:08:45,960
with exceptions like
Mr. Hair Plugs, of course.

210
00:08:47,962 --> 00:08:49,877
[Lisbon]
'You got the rebel
who took the bank job.'

211
00:08:51,574 --> 00:08:53,750
'The player that
stays faithful to his wife.'

212
00:08:53,837 --> 00:08:55,535
The rebel took the bank job
because she sees

213
00:08:55,622 --> 00:08:57,319
her rebellion is fruitless.

214
00:08:57,406 --> 00:08:59,626
The player stays faithful
to his wife

215
00:08:59,713 --> 00:09:01,410
because the consequence
of infidelity

216
00:09:01,497 --> 00:09:03,368
is much greater now.

217
00:09:03,455 --> 00:09:06,546
But their instincts, their
instinctsnever change.

218
00:09:06,633 --> 00:09:08,852
I'm a far cry from
what I was in high school.

219
00:09:08,939 --> 00:09:10,637
Yeah, I wouldn't be so sure.

220
00:09:10,724 --> 00:09:13,161
Driven to succeed to the point
of developing an ulcer.

221
00:09:13,248 --> 00:09:16,425
No tolerance for superiors
less sharp than yourself.

222
00:09:16,512 --> 00:09:18,949
Shutting out girls that
wanted to hang out with you.

223
00:09:19,036 --> 00:09:20,821
Blowing off boys
that want to get close.

224
00:09:20,908 --> 00:09:24,389
All the while,
at every turn, wondering

225
00:09:24,476 --> 00:09:27,175
what is it I really want?

226
00:09:27,262 --> 00:09:29,264
- No.
- And you played an instrument.

227
00:09:29,351 --> 00:09:32,484
My guess?
Hmm. Clarinet.

228
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,661
Not even close.
And we're done here.

229
00:09:34,748 --> 00:09:35,923
I'll get the guest list
to Rigsby.

230
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:37,011
I'll have him check
everybody out.

231
00:09:37,098 --> 00:09:38,055
Have him locate
the whereabouts

232
00:09:38,142 --> 00:09:40,101
of Derek Logan.

233
00:09:40,188 --> 00:09:43,017
Ah, you really think Logan
laid in wait for 15 years

234
00:09:43,104 --> 00:09:46,020
and suddenly decided
to take revenge on Selby?

235
00:09:46,107 --> 00:09:49,850
Well, I think that
Logan is as angry today

236
00:09:49,937 --> 00:09:53,070
as he was 15 years ago,
maybe even angrier.

237
00:09:53,157 --> 00:09:54,419
We'll check him out.

238
00:09:54,506 --> 00:09:55,420
You know, I'm gonna
stick around.

239
00:09:55,507 --> 00:09:56,813
I-I didn't go to high school

240
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:58,206
this is kind of
fascinatingfor me.

241
00:09:58,293 --> 00:09:59,511
You never went
to high school?

242
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:00,991
- No, I was busy.
- You can stay.

243
00:10:01,078 --> 00:10:02,514
Just don't
make me sorry I let you.

244
00:10:04,342 --> 00:10:05,300
Bassoon.

245
00:10:08,085 --> 00:10:09,826
Mrs. Vickers,
when was the last time

246
00:10:09,913 --> 00:10:10,827
you spoke to your son?

247
00:10:12,786 --> 00:10:14,352
Um, this morning.

248
00:10:14,439 --> 00:10:16,616
Selby always checks
in on me before he goes to work

249
00:10:16,703 --> 00:10:19,662
to see how I'm doing.
He's..

250
00:10:19,749 --> 00:10:21,359
He was sweet like that.

251
00:10:21,446 --> 00:10:23,057
