500
00:20:23,831 --> 00:20:25,224
One of the candidates lies.

501
00:20:26,573 --> 00:20:28,966
[instrumental music]

502
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,492
[knock on door]

503
00:20:37,671 --> 00:20:39,194
[Nyland]
'Yes?'

504
00:20:39,281 --> 00:20:41,327
It's agent Lisbon
and Patrick Jane.

505
00:20:41,414 --> 00:20:43,459
We just have a few
follow-up questions for you.

506
00:20:49,378 --> 00:20:51,119
Hi. How can I help?

507
00:20:51,206 --> 00:20:54,427
Last night at the reception,
you said you'd just gotten in

508
00:20:54,514 --> 00:20:57,604
but we know you flew
in the day before the murders.

509
00:20:57,691 --> 00:20:59,214
Can you explain
the discrepancy for us?

510
00:21:01,564 --> 00:21:02,652
Come on in.

511
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:07,266
I came a day early for
a private fundraising dinner.

512
00:21:08,963 --> 00:21:10,747
I said I'd just arrived
because I didn't want

513
00:21:10,834 --> 00:21:12,445
my classmates thinking

514
00:21:12,532 --> 00:21:14,882
I'm up here shilling
during reunion weekend.

515
00:21:14,969 --> 00:21:18,015
Nice room. Is it the, uh,
Presidential suite?

516
00:21:20,235 --> 00:21:22,281
Something like that.

517
00:21:22,368 --> 00:21:25,022
Is the bedroom nice?
How's the mattress?

518
00:21:25,109 --> 00:21:26,676
Uh, it's adequate.

519
00:21:26,763 --> 00:21:27,938
- Can I see it?
- Well, no.

520
00:21:28,025 --> 00:21:29,853
- Why would you want to?
- Why not?

521
00:21:29,940 --> 00:21:31,290
Because I'm entitled
to my privacy.

522
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:35,250
Hey!

523
00:21:36,512 --> 00:21:37,731
Whoa.

524
00:21:37,818 --> 00:21:38,949
Hello again.

525
00:21:39,863 --> 00:21:40,821
Hi.

526
00:21:50,091 --> 00:21:51,788
There was no inappropriate
relationship.

527
00:21:51,875 --> 00:21:54,008
You call it
an inappropriate relationship.

528
00:21:54,095 --> 00:21:57,403
The law calls it
soliciting sex from a minor.

529
00:21:57,490 --> 00:21:59,056
She came to my door.

530
00:21:59,143 --> 00:22:00,580
Had an idea
she wanted to discuss

531
00:22:00,667 --> 00:22:03,322
about a youth voter effort
for my campaign.

532
00:22:03,409 --> 00:22:05,149
I'm not going to discourage
some enthusiastic kid

533
00:22:05,236 --> 00:22:06,368
who wants to get involved.

534
00:22:06,455 --> 00:22:08,675
No, no. You hide 'em
in your bedroom.

535
00:22:08,762 --> 00:22:10,198
I had to.

536
00:22:10,285 --> 00:22:12,592
Media people follow me
everywhere I go now.

537
00:22:12,679 --> 00:22:14,855
If I open that door and it's
some guerrilla photographer

538
00:22:14,942 --> 00:22:16,030
our faces end up
on the internet

539
00:22:16,117 --> 00:22:17,640
both of our lives
are ruined.

540
00:22:17,727 --> 00:22:19,642
You're very good at this.

541
00:22:19,729 --> 00:22:23,429
Selling a case with passion,
even though it holds no water.

542
00:22:23,516 --> 00:22:25,300
Explains why you're
such a successful DA

543
00:22:26,562 --> 00:22:27,868
It's the truth.

544
00:22:27,955 --> 00:22:29,478
Well, that should
be easy to confirm.

545
00:22:29,565 --> 00:22:32,089
Lisbon, could you have
the social worker

546
00:22:32,176 --> 00:22:33,700
bring, uh, Tess in, please?

547
00:22:33,787 --> 00:22:34,962
No, please.

548
00:22:38,052 --> 00:22:41,098
This is on me.
She didn't ask for any of this.

549
00:22:41,185 --> 00:22:43,449
You care about her.

550
00:22:43,536 --> 00:22:46,016
You genuinely care
about her.

551
00:22:46,103 --> 00:22:47,931
Well, she's very friendly..

552
00:22:48,018 --> 00:22:49,237
...and diplomatic.

553
00:22:51,587 --> 00:22:53,241
Diplomatic..

554
00:22:53,328 --> 00:22:56,375
...and evasive,
like a politician..

555
00:22:56,462 --> 00:22:57,419
...like her father.

556
00:22:59,552 --> 00:23:01,597
That and you have
the same shape front teeth.

557
00:23:01,684 --> 00:23:03,338
They are your real teeth,
aren't they?

558
00:23:05,558 --> 00:23:06,907
[Lisbon]
'She's your daughter?'

559
00:23:11,477 --> 00:23:14,610
Her mother was
a year behind me.

560
00:23:14,697 --> 00:23:17,831
Tess was born a few weeks
before I graduated.

561
00:23:17,918 --> 00:23:20,399
Families agreed
to keep it quiet.

562
00:23:20,486 --> 00:23:21,878
But I've always done
right by Tess.

563
00:23:21,965 --> 00:23:24,141
Come out to see her
whenever I can.

564
00:23:24,228 --> 00:23:25,447
Discreetly, of course.

565
00:23:25,534 --> 00:23:28,319
Did you ever see, Selby
when you visited?

566
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:30,278
Last year, at a gas station
just outside of town

567
00:23:30,365 --> 00:23:32,976
We said a quick hello,
went our separate ways.

568
00:23:33,063 --> 00:23:35,326
Maybe Selby found
out about Tess.

569
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:36,893
Threatened to expose you.

570
00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:40,854
Not Selby Vickers.
He wouldn't threaten a fly.

571
00:23:40,941 --> 00:23:42,551
A super nice guy.

572
00:23:42,638 --> 00:23:44,248
He tried to do right
by people.

573
00:23:44,335 --> 00:23:46,294
What'd you talk about
with Selby at the gas station?

574
00:23:46,381 --> 00:23:48,383
Small talk. I told him,
I was gonna run

575
00:23:48,470 --> 00:23:50,516
for lieutenant governor
and he offered

576
00:23:50,603 --> 00:23:52,605
to print the campaign flyers,
free of charge.

577
00:23:52,692 --> 00:23:54,084
Was he the same way
in high school?

578
00:23:54,171 --> 00:23:56,609
Always.
Help you with your homework

579
00:23:56,696 --> 00:23:58,219
he'd share his lunch with you

580
00:23:58,306 --> 00:24:01,657
he was just happy
knowing that you liked him.

581
00:24:01,744 --> 00:24:06,009
Even that thing with Logan,
he just did it to be popular.

582
00:24:06,096 --> 00:24:08,969
I've answered
all your questions.

583
00:24:09,056 --> 00:24:10,144
I think you should go now.

584
00:24:14,496 --> 00:24:15,454
- Jane.
- What?

585
00:24:15,541 --> 00:24:17,543
- Come on.
- Oh, Sorry.

586
00:24:17,630 --> 00:24:19,109
Very nice to meet you.

587
00:24:19,196 --> 00:24:21,460
Your politics are a roiling mess
of greed and cynicism

588
00:24:21,547 --> 00:24:23,070
but you have
a lovely daughter.

589
00:24:26,552 --> 00:24:27,596
[Jason Gleed singing
"Follow Me Now"]

590
00:24:27,683 --> 00:24:30,033
♪ So everything's different ♪

591
00:24:30,120 --> 00:24:32,383
♪ I guess that's okay ♪

592
00:24:32,471 --> 00:24:34,908
♪ Cause those thoughts that used
to hold me down ♪

593
00:24:34,995 --> 00:24:37,214
♪ Have all gone away ♪

594
00:24:37,301 --> 00:24:40,435
♪ I feel like
I can take on the world ♪

595
00:24:40,522 --> 00:24:42,655
♪ So come along for the ride ♪

596
00:24:42,742 --> 00:24:45,309
♪ Or just get out of my way ♪

597
00:24:45,396 --> 00:24:48,095
♪ Come on Come on ♪♪

598
00:24:48,182 --> 00:24:50,140
[L.J.]
'Oh, him again.'

599
00:24:50,227 --> 00:24:53,622
Oh.

600
00:24:53,709 --> 00:24:54,667
I'll take care of it.

601
00:24:54,754 --> 00:24:55,885
Mm.

602
00:24:55,972 --> 00:24:58,279
[footsteps]

603
00:24:59,759 --> 00:25:01,587
Mr. Jane, hello.

604
00:25:01,674 --> 00:25:04,677
Willa, right?
Regional TV personality.

605
00:25:04,764 --> 00:25:06,461
Yes.

606
00:25:06,548 --> 00:25:08,768
Um, anything
I can help you with?

607
00:25:08,855 --> 00:25:10,509
Oh, I'm just here
for the big game.

608
00:25:10,596 --> 00:25:12,511
Football, I love it!

609
00:25:12,598 --> 00:25:14,208
How goes
the investigation?

610
00:25:14,295 --> 00:25:18,778
Oh, my colleagues are pursuing
several leads, uh..

611
00:25:18,865 --> 00:25:21,345
...nothing definitive yet.

612
00:25:21,432 --> 00:25:25,306
Mr. Jane, this is a weekend
of celebration.

613
00:25:25,393 --> 00:25:28,309
Your presence is making
a few people uncomfortable.

614
00:25:29,179 --> 00:25:30,529
Should I go away?

615
00:25:30,616 --> 00:25:36,752
Should I leave
Selby and Jana un-avenged

616
00:25:36,839 --> 00:25:38,667
because of some
low comfort levels?

617
00:25:38,754 --> 00:25:41,714
- Is that what you're saying?
- No, no.

618
00:25:41,801 --> 00:25:44,586
What are you saying then?

619
00:25:44,673 --> 00:25:46,806
I.. never mind.

620
00:25:46,893 --> 00:25:49,896
Okay.
Willa, I do have a question.

621
00:25:49,983 --> 00:25:52,855
- Yes?
- How are the burgers?

622
00:25:52,942 --> 00:25:54,117
The burg..

623
00:25:54,204 --> 00:25:56,337
The burgers
are good. Very good.

624
00:25:58,252 --> 00:26:01,037
[indistinct conversations]

625
00:26:12,005 --> 00:26:14,529
Vice principal DeSouza

626
00:26:14,616 --> 00:26:16,923
Do you mind
if I join you?

627
00:26:17,010 --> 00:26:19,926
Wow, look at you.
All grown-up.

628
00:26:20,013 --> 00:26:21,449
Sit down.

629
00:26:21,536 --> 00:26:23,712
Tell me what you've
been up to these days.

630
00:26:23,799 --> 00:26:25,366
Nice cover.

631
00:26:25,453 --> 00:26:27,281
I didn't actually attend
this high school.

632
00:26:27,368 --> 00:26:29,370
In fact, I didn't attend
any high school.

633
00:26:29,457 --> 00:26:30,414
I'm with the CBI.

634
00:26:30,501 --> 00:26:32,678
Oh, please, please.

635
00:26:32,765 --> 00:26:34,897
These reunions
are insufferable.

636
00:26:34,984 --> 00:26:37,378
What I wouldn't give
to be home on my couch

637
00:26:37,465 --> 00:26:41,121
glass of wine, good book.

638
00:26:41,208 --> 00:26:44,124
Well, I take it, you heard about
Selby Vickers and his wife.

639
00:26:44,211 --> 00:26:47,910
Oh, yes.
That's-that's a tragedy.

640
00:26:47,997 --> 00:26:50,652
Selby was a truly good kid.

641
00:26:50,739 --> 00:26:53,916
You know, until that one
incident with Derek Logan.

642
00:26:54,003 --> 00:26:56,136
Derek Logan was definitely
a different kinda duck.

643
00:26:56,223 --> 00:26:58,573
He wore the same tattered
jacket, be it hot or cold.

644
00:26:58,660 --> 00:27:01,228
Always hugged the wall
as he walked down a hallway.

645
00:27:01,315 --> 00:27:03,012
He was off.

646
00:27:03,099 --> 00:27:05,232
"off" isn't tolerated
in high school.

647
00:27:05,319 --> 00:27:08,235
Well, certainly not in the 30
years I've been doing this job.

648
00:27:13,109 --> 00:27:15,024
Right over there
is where it all happened.

649
00:27:17,244 --> 00:27:19,942
Derek's folks sent him to
a shrink afterwards.

650
00:27:20,029 --> 00:27:22,075
But it didn't help.

651
00:27:22,162 --> 00:27:24,033
A month later,
they pulled him out of school.

652
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:28,342
That was the last
I heard of him.

653
00:27:28,429 --> 00:27:29,386
Hmm.

654
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:41,050
Did Selby ever give
a reason why he did it?

655
00:27:41,137 --> 00:27:43,662
You know, I asked him,
but he just shrugged.

656
00:27:43,749 --> 00:27:47,840
You know, gave me that
teenage "I don't know."

657
00:27:49,102 --> 00:27:50,059
[sighs]

658
00:27:51,887 --> 00:27:53,715
How'd you catch him?

659
00:27:53,802 --> 00:27:55,195
Derek was blindfolded, right?

660
00:27:55,282 --> 00:27:58,546
Yes. He heard his attacker's
voice, though.

661
00:27:58,633 --> 00:28:01,114
He thought it sounded
like Selby.

662
00:28:01,201 --> 00:28:03,594
I confronted Selby.
He confessed quite readily

663
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:07,947
like the helpful,
honest boy he usually was.

664
00:28:08,034 --> 00:28:09,339
It's very strange.

665
00:28:12,560 --> 00:28:14,867
Hmm..

666
00:28:14,954 --> 00:28:16,869
You want me to memorize
everything we have

667
00:28:16,956 --> 00:28:19,262
on all 67 alumni
that showed up to the reunion?

668
00:28:19,349 --> 00:28:20,394
Yes, I do.

669
00:28:20,481 --> 00:28:22,091
And how would I do that?

670
00:28:22,178 --> 00:28:24,485
It's easy.
You build a memory palace.

671
00:28:24,572 --> 00:28:26,574
Um, I thought that was just
some card player's trick.

672
00:28:26,661 --> 00:28:28,315
Well, it's multipurpose.

673
00:28:28,402 --> 00:28:30,883
It's perfect for recalling
a large body of information.

674
00:28:30,970 --> 00:28:34,190
All you need is a physical
location that you know well.

675
00:28:34,277 --> 00:28:37,672
And you break it down in your
mind into smaller pieces

676
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:42,633
and link each one to a package
of the information..

677
00:28:42,721 --> 00:28:43,765
Like this.

678
00:28:47,595 --> 00:28:50,250
I walk in the door

679
00:28:50,337 --> 00:28:54,123
and I'm greeted by
reunion chair, Willa Brock.

680
00:28:54,210 --> 00:28:56,691
Former class president,
debate team captain

681
00:28:56,778 --> 00:28:59,215
led the team to
three county championships.

682
00:28:59,302 --> 00:29:01,522
Now a talk show host
in Chicago.

683
00:29:01,609 --> 00:29:04,351
I sit down at the table
and catch up

684
00:29:04,438 --> 00:29:08,355
with Dana Greer, swimmer,
now a realtor in Los Angeles

685
00:29:08,442 --> 00:29:10,487
married to a gentleman
by the name of Arthur.

686
00:29:10,574 --> 00:29:12,315
And so on and so forth.

687
00:29:12,402 --> 00:29:13,708
Okay.

688
00:29:13,795 --> 00:29:16,189
When you want to
remember the details

689
00:29:16,276 --> 00:29:19,845
you close your eyes,
and in your mind

690
00:29:19,932 --> 00:29:22,761
you walk around
your very own memory palace.

691
00:29:25,111 --> 00:29:27,548
Yeah, but I-I can't learn all
this in just a couple of hours.

692
00:29:27,635 --> 00:29:29,332
It comes very quickly
once you get the hang of it

693
00:29:29,419 --> 00:29:31,247
and they'll be
wearing nametags.

694
00:29:31,334 --> 00:29:32,814
But why? I mean,
why would I memorize all these--

695
00:29:32,901 --> 00:29:33,815
It's fun.

696
00:29:35,904 --> 00:29:37,732
This is some dubious scheme
that Lisbon doesn't know about

697
00:29:37,819 --> 00:29:39,734
isn't it?
Yeah, you can count me out.

698
00:29:40,822 --> 00:29:41,954
Sorry, you gotta do it.

699
00:29:42,041 --> 00:29:43,303
Uh, no, I don't.

700
00:29:47,742 --> 00:29:49,396
If you, uh, don't co-operate

701
00:29:49,483 --> 00:29:52,312
I maybe forced to tell
Lisbon about you and Van Pelt.

702
00:29:52,399 --> 00:29:54,836
Tell what?
There's nothing to tell.

703
00:29:57,752 --> 00:29:59,188
Really?

704
00:29:59,275 --> 00:30:01,408
Yeah. I don't know
what you're talking about.

705
00:30:01,495 --> 00:30:03,497
Ah.

706
00:30:03,584 --> 00:30:05,978
Contrary to very strict
CBI rules and regulations

707
00:30:06,065 --> 00:30:12,201
you and Grace Van Pelt are
engaged in an illicit affair.

708
00:30:12,288 --> 00:30:14,029
Nope.

709
00:30:14,116 --> 00:30:16,292
You're being childish.

710
00:30:18,033 --> 00:30:19,295
Don't tell Lisbon.
She'll report us to HR.

711
00:30:19,382 --> 00:30:20,514
Well, she's a stickler.

712
00:30:20,601 --> 00:30:21,645
They'll throw one of us
off the unit.

713
00:30:21,732 --> 00:30:23,038
Better get to work.

714
00:30:24,692 --> 00:30:26,694
[Los Del Rio singing
"Macarena"]

715
00:30:26,781 --> 00:30:29,088
♪ Hey, macarena, ay! ♪

716
00:30:29,175 --> 00:30:31,133
♪ Dale a tu cuerpo
alegria macarena ♪

717
00:30:31,220 --> 00:30:33,919
♪ Que tu cuerpo es pa' darle
alegria y cosa buena ♪

718
00:30:34,006 --> 00:30:36,008
♪ Dale a tu cuerpo
alegria macarena ♪

719
00:30:36,095 --> 00:30:38,314
♪ Hey macarena, ay! ♪

720
00:30:38,401 --> 00:30:40,447
♪ Macarena tiene un novio
que se llama ♪

721
00:30:40,534 --> 00:30:42,666
♪ Que se llama
de apellido vitorino ♪

722
00:30:42,753 --> 00:30:45,365
♪ Que en la jura
de bandera el muchacho ♪

723
00:30:45,452 --> 00:30:47,715
♪ Es pa' darle
alegria y cosa buena ♪

724
00:30:47,802 --> 00:30:49,543
♪ Dale a tu cuerpo
alegria macarena ♪

725
00:30:49,630 --> 00:30:51,806
♪ Hey macarena, ay! ♪

726
00:30:51,893 --> 00:30:53,416
School would be
so much more fun

727
00:30:53,503 --> 00:30:55,462
if they started the day
with this every morning

728
00:30:55,549 --> 00:30:58,247
instead of the, uh,
pledge of allegiance.

729
00:30:58,334 --> 00:31:00,684
Or maybe they could, uh,
just integrate the two

730
00:31:00,771 --> 00:31:04,210
into the "dance of allegiance."

731
00:31:04,297 --> 00:31:06,908
We're taking a real flier here.
This better work.

732
00:31:06,995 --> 00:31:09,345
- Timpani.
- No.

733
00:31:09,432 --> 00:31:11,782
Huh. Really got me stumped
on that one.

734
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:13,262
I'm just guessing now.

735
00:31:13,349 --> 00:31:14,307
We'd better get
this thing going

736
00:31:14,394 --> 00:31:15,830
before people start leaving.

737
00:31:15,917 --> 00:31:18,180
Have patience.
The fun will commence shortly.

738
00:31:20,791 --> 00:31:22,576
[Ini Kamoze singing
"Hotstepper"]

739
00:31:22,663 --> 00:31:25,405
♪ Na, na-na-na, na ♪

740
00:31:25,492 --> 00:31:27,581
Hey, how's it going?

741
00:31:27,668 --> 00:31:28,625
Nice to see you.

742
00:31:28,712 --> 00:31:29,670
Long time.

743
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:32,194
Hey.

744
00:31:35,502 --> 00:31:37,373
Coffee machine.

745
00:31:39,854 --> 00:31:41,769
Stu McAlpine?

746
00:31:41,856 --> 00:31:45,251
How goes it with my favorite
photo club president?

747
00:31:45,338 --> 00:31:47,122
It goes great.
How goes it with you?

748
00:31:47,209 --> 00:31:49,037
It goes whatever's
better than great.

749
00:31:49,124 --> 00:31:51,344
You know,
I-I forgot your name.

750
00:31:51,431 --> 00:31:54,608
It's, uh...
Derek Logan.

751
00:31:54,695 --> 00:31:56,697
Yeah.

752
00:31:59,482 --> 00:32:00,614
It's great to be back.

753
00:32:02,616 --> 00:32:06,054
♪♪

754
00:32:06,141 --> 00:32:07,447
Hi.

755
00:32:07,534 --> 00:32:08,622
How are you?

756
00:32:08,709 --> 00:32:09,928
Hi.

757
00:32:13,192 --> 00:32:15,585
Oh, yeah.

758
00:32:15,672 --> 00:32:18,327
This is gonna be good.

759
00:32:18,414 --> 00:32:19,807
I promise.

760
00:32:24,986 --> 00:32:26,205
Great to see you, too, man.

761
00:32:26,292 --> 00:32:28,337
Derek Logan.
I-I can't believe it.

762
00:32:28,424 --> 00:32:30,035
Yeah, you've changed.

763
00:32:30,122 --> 00:32:31,775
Well, who would've thought
that the girl who brought

764
00:32:31,862 --> 00:32:33,168
four schools to their knees

765
00:32:33,255 --> 00:32:34,300
in the high school
county debate finals

766
00:32:34,387 --> 00:32:35,605
would be lost for words, huh?

767
00:32:35,692 --> 00:32:38,043
You-you just
look so different.

768
00:32:38,130 --> 00:32:40,654
Let's just chalk it up to
15 years' worth of solid hours

769
00:32:40,741 --> 00:32:43,309
at the health club,
plus maybe a little bit of work.

770
00:32:43,396 --> 00:32:45,050
You gotta look good
in my business, huh?

771
00:32:45,137 --> 00:32:49,228
- You know what I mean?
- See it to believe it. Derek.

772
00:32:49,315 --> 00:32:50,838
Hey, L.J., hey!

773
00:32:50,925 --> 00:32:52,579
- Refrigerator.
- What?

774
00:32:52,666 --> 00:32:54,494
Rancho Rosa versus Stratton.

775
00:32:54,581 --> 00:32:57,410
The ball is on our 10,
2 seconds on the clock

776
00:32:57,497 --> 00:32:59,107
Sims hands it off, bam!

777
00:32:59,194 --> 00:33:02,458
You run 90 yards,
touchdown, Toros win.

778
00:33:02,545 --> 00:33:03,677
Oh, you're-you're half right.

779
00:33:03,764 --> 00:33:05,113
That was against Deerfield.

780
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,115
And it was a pass,
not a handoff

781
00:33:07,202 --> 00:33:10,684
but it was close. Man!
That's Derek freakin' Logan!

782
00:33:10,771 --> 00:33:12,468
Whoo!

783
00:33:12,555 --> 00:33:14,601
I'm gonna, uh, make the rounds
to say some hellos

784
00:33:14,688 --> 00:33:16,690
but it is great
to see you guys.

785
00:33:16,777 --> 00:33:17,952
Wow!

786
00:33:19,345 --> 00:33:22,130
[indistinct conversations]

787
00:33:22,217 --> 00:33:24,350
- Wow, you're a natural.
- I can't do this.

788
00:33:24,437 --> 00:33:25,786
You're doing it.

789
00:33:25,873 --> 00:33:28,528
- You're ready for phase two?
- I can't.

790
00:33:28,615 --> 00:33:31,052
Think of it like this,
you mess up, we blow the case

791
00:33:31,139 --> 00:33:32,488
might tell Lisbon.

792
00:33:32,575 --> 00:33:34,577
Oh, you're
a cold bastard, you know that?

793
00:33:34,664 --> 00:33:36,536
[female# 1]
'Good evening, fellow Toros!'

794
00:33:36,623 --> 00:33:38,059
[applauding]

795
00:33:41,062 --> 00:33:44,109
Now is the part of the evening
you've all been waiting for

796
00:33:44,196 --> 00:33:46,328
the achievement awards!

797
00:33:46,415 --> 00:33:47,808
[applauding]

798
00:33:50,158 --> 00:33:51,986
As voted by you

799
00:33:52,073 --> 00:33:55,772
the 15th reunion class of
Rancho Rosa high.

800
00:33:55,859 --> 00:33:57,209
[cheering]

801
00:33:59,602 --> 00:34:00,734
Break a leg.

802
00:34:00,821 --> 00:34:02,562
[Willa]
'Our first award.'

803
00:34:02,649 --> 00:34:05,521
The "I can't believe
they're still together" award

804
00:34:05,608 --> 00:34:06,827
which goes to

805
00:34:06,914 --> 00:34:08,524
Dave Mercer
and Angie Diaz Mercer.

806
00:34:08,611 --> 00:34:10,831
No surprises there,
am I right, gang?

807
00:34:10,918 --> 00:34:12,659
What are you doing?

808
00:34:12,746 --> 00:34:13,964
I'm a let you finish, Willa.

809
00:34:14,052 --> 00:34:15,966
I, uh, just want to say
a few quick words.

810
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:17,185
Okay.
Just make it fast--

811
00:34:17,272 --> 00:34:18,230
- Sure.
- Okay.

812
00:34:18,317 --> 00:34:19,753
Uh, slight change of schedule.

813
00:34:19,840 --> 00:34:20,797
We'll get right back to
the awards

814
00:34:20,884 --> 00:34:25,193
but first, Derek Logan!

815
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:26,238
[applauding]

816
00:34:26,325 --> 00:34:27,456
[male #1]
Yo, D!

817
00:34:27,543 --> 00:34:29,502
Yeah.

818
00:34:29,589 --> 00:34:31,982
Mm, uh, sure most of you are
scratching your heads

819
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:35,029
wondering why, uh,
why I'm here.

820
00:34:35,116 --> 00:34:37,684
I came here tonight
because, uh...

821
00:34:37,771 --> 00:34:40,687
Wanted to see how it felt like
to be here again.

822
00:34:40,774 --> 00:34:43,168
'I'm not the same person
I was 15 years ago'

823
00:34:43,255 --> 00:34:44,734
so when I walked in
that front door tonight..

824
00:34:44,821 --> 00:34:45,779
...felt good.

825
00:34:45,866 --> 00:34:48,129
[applauding]

826
00:34:48,216 --> 00:34:49,696
Thank you.

827
00:34:49,783 --> 00:34:54,092
But as soon as I set my eyes
on you people

828
00:34:54,179 --> 00:34:57,443
I remember how it felt the last
time I walked out that door.

829
00:34:57,530 --> 00:35:01,577
And I was that
sad, defeated kid again.

830
00:35:01,664 --> 00:35:05,364
Sure, go ahead.
Feel sorry for me.

831
00:35:05,451 --> 00:35:07,496
You should also
feel sorry for Selby.

832
00:35:07,583 --> 00:35:10,369
May he, uh,
rest in peace.

833
00:35:10,456 --> 00:35:13,763
'About a month ago,
Selby called me.'

834
00:35:13,850 --> 00:35:16,288
'He'd been, uh, trying to track
me down for months, he said.'

835
00:35:16,375 --> 00:35:18,942
'He wanted to apologize'

836
00:35:19,029 --> 00:35:23,773
'and tell the truth about
what really happened that day.'

837
00:35:23,860 --> 00:35:26,689
'The truth
that never came out.'

838
00:35:26,776 --> 00:35:28,909
'You see,
Selby was a follower.'

839
00:35:28,996 --> 00:35:29,910
Not a leader.

840
00:35:29,997 --> 00:35:31,433
'And he did what he did'

841
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:34,088
'because somebody else
was there that day.'

842
00:35:34,175 --> 00:35:35,698
somebody told him
to do what he did to me.

843
00:35:35,785 --> 00:35:38,397
Yeah, that's right.

844
00:35:38,484 --> 00:35:40,355
Hey, Gina, what's up?

845
00:35:42,227 --> 00:35:46,318
He'll be fine. Just, um, uh...
give him an aspirin.

846
00:35:46,405 --> 00:35:49,625
And I now know, who it was.

847
00:35:49,712 --> 00:35:53,020
And that is the real reason
I am here.

848
00:35:53,107 --> 00:35:55,805
I'm here to make you pay.

849
00:35:55,892 --> 00:35:57,024
[murmuring]

850
00:35:57,111 --> 00:35:59,809
Yeah, you-you ruined my life..

851
00:35:59,896 --> 00:36:01,811
'...uh, that day.'

852
00:36:01,898 --> 00:36:05,337
And I've spent 15 years
struggling to get it back.

853
00:36:05,424 --> 00:36:07,774
And now, now I have.
Oh, yeah.

854
00:36:07,861 --> 00:36:10,516
And I will have my revenge.

855
00:36:10,603 --> 00:36:13,258
Payback is-is-is a bitch.

856
00:36:13,345 --> 00:36:16,348
'like, uh, in that movie
with, um, uh...'

857
00:36:16,435 --> 00:36:17,566
With uh,
Mel-Mel Gibson where they..

858
00:36:17,653 --> 00:36:19,046
...where they kidnap his child.

859
00:36:19,133 --> 00:36:21,091
Um, you know.
Uh, or is it the other one?

860
00:36:21,179 --> 00:36:25,183
Uh, anyhow, um, that's me.
Enjoy the rest of your evening.

861
00:36:25,270 --> 00:36:27,620
Go, Toros.

862
00:36:27,707 --> 00:36:31,058
[applauding]

863
00:36:31,145 --> 00:36:33,191
What-what do you
think you're doing?

864
00:36:33,278 --> 00:36:34,931
Oh, the maid lent us this.

865
00:36:35,018 --> 00:36:37,499
You still should tip her.
It's the right thing to do.

866
00:36:37,586 --> 00:36:38,979
Must've been hard walking out

867
00:36:39,066 --> 00:36:41,851
in the middle of
a big event you planned.

868
00:36:41,938 --> 00:36:44,941
The speech was boring and I have
to get back to Chicago.

869
00:36:45,028 --> 00:36:48,293
I have two shows
to prepare for on Monday.

870
00:36:48,380 --> 00:36:49,903
I have a great idea
for your show.

871
00:36:49,990 --> 00:36:54,908
Uh, "humiliating pranks and the
people who initiate them."

872
00:36:54,995 --> 00:36:56,388
You could be
your own guest.

873
00:36:56,475 --> 00:36:58,128
[laughing]

874
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:00,479
You-you have
no basis for that.

875
00:37:00,566 --> 00:37:03,699
I just- I didn't want to have to
hear Derek go on and on about--

876
00:37:03,786 --> 00:37:06,659
Your talk show
goes national soon.

877
00:37:06,746 --> 00:37:08,443
So?

878
00:37:08,530 --> 00:37:10,880
If Selby had gone to the media
with the story of

879
00:37:10,967 --> 00:37:13,535
how you brutalized
a helpless boy

880
00:37:13,622 --> 00:37:16,799
your big chance
would be history.

881
00:37:16,886 --> 00:37:21,195
'So you arranged a meeting
with Selby to get the money.'

882
00:37:21,282 --> 00:37:22,892
[Teresa]
'Jana showed up with him,
which you weren't expecting'

883
00:37:22,979 --> 00:37:24,503
'so you killed them both.'

884
00:37:24,590 --> 00:37:28,985
Oh, okay, I-I didn't have to
pay him or kill him.

885
00:37:29,072 --> 00:37:31,727
[Willa]
'I, Selby didn't have
a stitch of proof'

886
00:37:31,814 --> 00:37:34,034
'putting me
in that locker room.'

887
00:37:34,121 --> 00:37:37,124
The media would've ignored him
as a crackpot.

888
00:37:37,211 --> 00:37:41,171
"I have immortal longings
in me."

889
00:37:41,259 --> 00:37:43,609
Do you remember that quote?

890
00:37:43,696 --> 00:37:45,611
- Uh, uh, it's Shakespeare.
- Uh-huh.

891
00:37:45,698 --> 00:37:49,484
I-I think it was the quote
in my yearbook photo.

892
00:37:49,571 --> 00:37:51,094
And an apt one.

893
00:37:51,181 --> 00:37:53,662
High school was a wonderful time
for you, wasn't it?

894
00:37:53,749 --> 00:37:55,273
Yeah, you could say that.

895
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:58,754
Star student, class president,
champion debater.

896
00:37:58,841 --> 00:38:00,887
You were at the top
of the social hierarchy.

897
00:38:00,974 --> 00:38:02,497
Willa Brock was
the queen of the school.

898
00:38:02,584 --> 00:38:05,979
Your world was perfect.

899
00:38:06,066 --> 00:38:08,068
- Yes.
- Yeah.

900
00:38:08,155 --> 00:38:09,199
But then something happened

901
00:38:09,287 --> 00:38:11,027
and unsettled
that perfect world.

902
00:38:11,114 --> 00:38:15,945
Derek Logan irked you,
somehow.

903
00:38:16,032 --> 00:38:18,339
And you just couldn't let it
pass without a response

904
00:38:18,426 --> 00:38:19,993
so you turned on the charm

905
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:22,125
you manipulated Selby
to do your bidding

906
00:38:22,212 --> 00:38:25,172
knowing that he'd be thrilled
to help the popular girl.

907
00:38:25,259 --> 00:38:29,611
The girl he was always
a little in love with.

908
00:38:29,698 --> 00:38:31,918
And then you destroyed
Derek Logan.

909
00:38:32,005 --> 00:38:34,224
To the delight
of your peers.

910
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,357
'And you enjoyed it.'

911
00:38:36,444 --> 00:38:40,579
'cause you found it all
so easy and so empowering

912
00:38:40,666 --> 00:38:44,670
and exciting, right?

913
00:38:44,757 --> 00:38:47,107
All your success
at Rancho Rosa high.

914
00:38:47,194 --> 00:38:49,152
This..

915
00:38:49,239 --> 00:38:52,155
'...was Willa Brock's
crowning achievement.'

916
00:38:58,858 --> 00:39:00,338
[whistles]

917
00:39:02,078 --> 00:39:03,297
You've aged well.

918
00:39:05,734 --> 00:39:07,823
It looks like Selby
took more than one photo

919
00:39:07,910 --> 00:39:10,522
that day in the locker room,
didn't he?

920
00:39:10,609 --> 00:39:11,871
Have a look at that.

921
00:39:11,958 --> 00:39:14,395
Check that out.

922
00:39:29,236 --> 00:39:33,632
[clicking]

923
00:39:38,767 --> 00:39:41,553
This is Selby's proof.

924
00:39:41,640 --> 00:39:42,989
But you didn't want to
pay him all that money

925
00:39:43,076 --> 00:39:44,991
and risk him
blackmailing you again.

926
00:39:45,078 --> 00:39:48,386
So you killed him
and his wife Jana.

927
00:39:51,519 --> 00:39:55,262
Kinda poetic, how you were
done in by your own vanity.

928
00:39:57,917 --> 00:40:02,051
Derek Logan told everyone
I let him touch me.

929
00:40:02,138 --> 00:40:05,490
Like I ever would.

930
00:40:05,577 --> 00:40:07,405
I was deeply humiliated.

931
00:40:07,492 --> 00:40:09,407
So you ruined his life.

932
00:40:09,494 --> 00:40:12,584
And Selby and Jana Vickers
had to die, too.

933
00:40:12,671 --> 00:40:15,108
Selby falls for
that little polish girl

934
00:40:15,195 --> 00:40:18,851
and suddenly grows a spine?

935
00:40:18,938 --> 00:40:20,287
Things would have been perfect

936
00:40:20,374 --> 00:40:24,160
if he just stayed
lonely and pathetic.

937
00:40:25,510 --> 00:40:27,642
Close call.
If she'd have destroyed

938
00:40:27,729 --> 00:40:29,296
the negative that Selby
had given her

939
00:40:29,383 --> 00:40:31,080
we'd have no evidence
and no case.

940
00:40:31,167 --> 00:40:32,647
It was a trophy.

941
00:40:32,734 --> 00:40:34,301
It was a reminder
that the great Willa Brock

942
00:40:34,388 --> 00:40:36,085
can crush anyone
that dares stand in her way

943
00:40:36,172 --> 00:40:37,783
just like 15 years ago.

944
00:40:37,870 --> 00:40:40,481
Yes, yes. Nobody advances
an inch from high school.

945
00:40:40,568 --> 00:40:42,962
- You proved your point.
- Their instincts never change.

946
00:40:46,792 --> 00:40:48,663
Selby and Derek
would both be grateful.

947
00:40:48,750 --> 00:40:50,099
You two have
an open invitation

948
00:40:50,186 --> 00:40:52,450
if you want to
join us at the 20th.

949
00:40:52,537 --> 00:40:54,669
Hopefully,
we won't need to.

950
00:40:54,756 --> 00:40:57,672
Keep it in the dojo, Phil.

951
00:40:57,759 --> 00:40:59,326
One thing I don't get.

952
00:40:59,413 --> 00:41:02,285
How did you persuade Rigsby
to play this charade?

953
00:41:02,372 --> 00:41:06,333
I told him that you promised
to give him Monday off.

954
00:41:06,420 --> 00:41:09,075
Not happening.

955
00:41:10,729 --> 00:41:13,819
Well, that puts me
in an awkward position.

956
00:41:13,906 --> 00:41:15,647
I-I-I-I held up my end
of the bargain.

957
00:41:15,734 --> 00:41:17,213
[Extreme singing
"More Than Words"]

958
00:41:17,300 --> 00:41:22,088
- Oh, god. I loved this song.
- Loved this song.

959
00:41:22,175 --> 00:41:24,090
- I used to love this song.
- You love this song.

960
00:41:24,177 --> 00:41:27,310
- Yeah.
- Obviously, you want to dance.

961
00:41:27,397 --> 00:41:29,748
- With you? No.
- Oh, come on.

962
00:41:29,835 --> 00:41:32,446
You can pretend that
I'm that mean, cold-hearted guy

963
00:41:32,533 --> 00:41:36,145
that you used to worship
from afar, but never talked to.

964
00:41:36,232 --> 00:41:39,584
♪ How easy it would be ♪

965
00:41:39,671 --> 00:41:40,715
Hmm.

966
00:41:40,802 --> 00:41:41,716
No funny stuff.

967
00:41:43,588 --> 00:41:47,200
Really?

968
00:41:47,287 --> 00:41:50,246
♪ More than words ♪

969
00:41:50,333 --> 00:41:53,467
♪ Is all you have to do ♪

970
00:41:53,554 --> 00:41:56,905
♪ To make it real ♪

971
00:41:56,992 --> 00:42:00,126
♪ Then you wouldn't
have to say ♪

972
00:42:00,213 --> 00:42:02,041
Trumpet?

973
00:42:02,128 --> 00:42:04,086
♪ That you love me ♪

974
00:42:04,173 --> 00:42:05,566
No.

975
00:42:05,653 --> 00:42:11,746
♪ 'Cause I'd already know ♪♪

976
00:42:14,009 --> 00:42:16,751
Stay tuned for
scenes from our next episode.

977
00:42:20,712 --> 00:42:23,105
[theme music]

